{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_obligation.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));cid=r['candidates'][0]['id'];q=r['candidates'][0]['question']\nq['unknowns']=['Can a fixed, fully drained periodic suffix demonstrate recurrence of all behavior-determining state after transfer abort, excluding an outstanding internal continuation?','Does the fixed monitor preserve the distinction between non-completion over finite ticks and a repeatable execution with no autonomous exit?']\nq['counterevidence']=['Automatic exit succeeds when the same change is applied without transfer overlap in exploration 4cefa9ac8b454a8891e746a89558055c.','A later ordinary proposal causes application progress and automatic exit in the transfer case; this bounds the failure to absence of unrelated new application work.','Existing TestRawNodeJointAutoLeave covers a new election followed by new applied entries, another recovery path outside stable retained leadership.','Exploration is not fixed property evidence; a finite tick window alone does not prove lost continuation.']\nq['disposition']='ready_for_check'\nq['trigger_rationale']='Exploration reached the actual committed-change/application/transfer overlap through public APIs. Transfer cleared at tick 10, while joint AutoLeave remained at tick 40 with queues and Ready work drained. A later ordinary command restored exit. Source callers of appliedTo are entry application and snapshot completion; abort itself does not retry. A fixed full-state recurrence check can distinguish an autonomous delayed continuation from the observed trigger dependency.'\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v1.json'))\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='B-autoleave':\n  b['important_branches']=['When transfer rejects the internal leave proposal, no leave entry is appended and AutoLeave remains true. Retry is reevaluated on later appliedTo entry/snapshot completion; a message-only synchronous Advance schedules no such callback.']\n  b['unknowns']=['Whether an application-free heartbeat/tick execution after abort preserves all behavior-determining state across a complete timer period']\n  b['source_ids']=sorted(set(b['source_ids']+['S-advance','S-dispatch','S-abort']))\n if b['id']=='B-transfer':\n  b['important_branches']=['Timeout abort clears leadTransferee without invoking application completion or internal configuration proposal. Subsequent new application progress can independently invoke appliedTo.']\n  b['unknowns']=[]\nm['core_overview']['open_details']=[('Repeatable application-free suffix after failed transfer' if x=='Automatic joint exit retry following failed transfer' else x) for x in m['core_overview']['open_details']]\nm['core_overview']['connection']['explanation']=m['core_overview']['connection']['explanation'].replace('Application completion can propose automatic joint exit, but transfer admission can reject that proposal; these local continuation questions do not prevent understanding the backbone.','Application completion can propose automatic joint exit, but transfer admission can reject that proposal. Timeout abort clears the transfer field without rescheduling this action; subsequent applied entries or snapshot completion reevaluate it. Whether an application-free periodic suffix remains closed is a local continuation question.')\njson.dump(m,open('map-autoleave.json','w'),indent=2)\nclaim='C-auto-exit-continuation'\nsources=['S-jointcontract','S-autoleave-tracker-contract','S-autoleave','S-proposal','S-ticks','S-abort','S-advance','S-nodecontract','S-storage']\ng=dict(source_ids=sources,expectation_ids=['S-jointcontract','S-autoleave-tracker-contract'],derivation='ConfChangeTransitionJointImplicit specifies automatic exit by a zero configuration proposal; ConfState.AutoLeave and tracker.Config explicitly assign this transition to Raft when possible, contrasting explicit mode where the application must propose it. The application already proposed and applied the entering configuration. appliedTo implements the internal continuation and explicitly anticipates rejection during transfer and a later retry. This establishes implementation ownership beyond the word automatic alone. Under retained leadership and a viable joint quorum after transfer abort, absence of an unrelated client command must not permanently eliminate that continuation. Generic caller retry duties for external proposals do not require inventing new client work to drive an already applied automatic transition. No numeric deadline is claimed; only a closed repeating execution without an internally driven transition would witness the requirement gap.',applicability='Committed implicit joint change applied in order; transfer overlaps its application acknowledgment and later aborts; eligible leader retained, viable incoming/outgoing quorums, reliable ongoing ordinary message delivery and ticks, storage/application work completed; no crash or new client commands.',alternatives=['A later committed application callback legitimately retries and may recover; a new leader may generate such progress with its empty entry. These do not promise an event in the stable-leader, application-free suffix.'],unresolved=['Fixed recurrence observations and semantic correspondence have not yet been executed/reviewed.'])\nc=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='bounded_liveness',description='After an implicit joint configuration has been committed and applied, Raft must retain or restore an internally driven continuation to leave the joint configuration when an overlapping leadership transfer aborts, provided leadership and a viable joint quorum remain stable and required storage, application, ticks and network work continue. Completing that automatic transition must not depend on an unrelated new client proposal.',source_ids=sources,scope=dict(description='Implementation-owned automatic joint-exit continuation under an aborted